# play.mdc — Play Framework stack rules (optional per repository)

Define **repo-specific** Play upgrade paths and verification here. Agents read this **only** when listed in `codingStandards.documentation.stackRules` — the kit does **not** hardcode Play or Lombok rules.

```yaml
playStack:
  targetVersion: TBD
  upgradeFrom:
    playVersion: TBD
    runtimeVersion: TBD

  paths:
    routes: conf/routes
    controllers: app/controllers
    services: app/services
    models: app/models
    tests: test/

  buildFiles: []  # e.g. build.sbt, project/plugins.sbt

  migrations: []  # repo-specific — from official Play migration guide + SDD

  verify: []  # repo-specific checks before compile (grep patterns, coordinate pins, etc.)
```

**Agent rule:** Play changes require scope per SDD — not build files alone. Run `playStack.verify` from **this file** at [project-context-sync](../../sdlc-system/workflow/project-context-sync.md). **Compile** proves compatibility ([pre-pr-verification.md](../../sdlc-system/workflow/pre-pr-verification.md)).
